  "system": {
    "description": "<p>Spindles are wound lengths of thin (0.2 millimeters) but super-strong fullerene cable. It can extend 250 meters of cable capable of supporting 5,000 kilograms of weight at 1 g. The spindle also contains a specialized fabber that can manufacture more cable and extend it indefinitely, at a rate of 1 meter per minute, as long as it is fed with raw materials. The spindle can cut the cables it produces at any length. If fixed in place with built-in grip pads, it can also retract the cable at a rate of 50 meters per action turn, or re-absorb cables at the rate of 5 meters per minute. Spindle cables can be cut by inflicting 30 points of damage.</p>",
    "reference": "Eclipse Phase Second Edition p. 341",
